WEBVTT

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:10.610
Ren, what are you doing?

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.440
It's this floss.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.950
Sorry. They didn't have 
your usual floss at the store.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.670
Open your mouth.

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:21.200
I'm not a child. I can do it myself.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.210
<i>There it is! Ren's "I can do it myself"!</i>

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:27.670
I know you can, but it's hard to use, right?

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:28.660
Yeah.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.710
Just look at those canines. 
No wonder the floss broke.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.230
I'll buy you some of your 
usual floss tomorrow...

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:37.720
What?

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.410
You have a tooth right here!

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:41.470
Of course I do.

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:44.730
That's not what I meant! 
Remember, last year in Canada...

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.360
My tooth fell out.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:52.060
I'm sorry, Ren! The bacon must've been too hard.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.110
We need to get you to a dentist right away!

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:55.640
It's not a problem.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.070
How is that not a problem?!

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.080
It's small. Is this...

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.080
It's a milk tooth. 
That's why it's not a problem.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.790
A baby tooth! Baby tooth!

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:08.640
It's a milk tooth! 
Don't call it a baby tooth!

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.710
I remember that happening.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.610
Ren, go see the dentist tomorrow.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:15.220
Why?

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:19.810
I've been meaning to send you to 
a dentist since you came to Japan.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:22.220
I don't like dentists. 
I don't have any cavities.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:23.470
Ren...

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:28.230
If you're not a child, then you must 
not be scared of the dentist, right?

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:30.320
Who said I'm scared?

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.230
I just said I don't like dentists.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.580
Ren, did you know?

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:37.240
Tooth decay can spread to 
other people through a kiss.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:41.450
Well, if you really don't 
want to go, then it's fine.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:45.220
It just means I won't be able to kiss 
my dear Ren for the foreseeable future.

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:46.000
Wha—

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.720
How sad.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:54.000
<i>He really didn't kiss my mouth that time.</i>

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:27.480
I'm home.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:28.460
Welcome back.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.910
Ren, do you want pancakes for a snack?

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.260
No, I'm good.

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:37.810
Brother, I bought the dental floss.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:38.860
Is this the right one?

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.730
Yeah, that's it. Thanks, Shima.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.220
Anyway, what's gotten into Ren?

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.080
I was going to ask you that.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.370
He suddenly asked me to make 
a dentist appointment for him.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:50.870
Ren did?

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.830
I called them, but I couldn't get an 
appointment until the end of next week.

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:56.820
Does Ren Ren have a cavity?

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.820
He's not you.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:02.840
It's just a checkup. I told him 
he should go at least once.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.250
Oh...

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:06.400
I'm home.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.850
I'm hungry. Give me something to eat.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:10.850
Sorry, Aki and Shima.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:12.680
Could you look after things here?

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:13.360
Huh?

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:14.850
Okay.

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:20.190
Ren.

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:24.740
Hey, uh... It's not good for your 
teeth to brush them so much.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:26.700
Really?

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.450
Didn't you get a dentist appointment?

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:31.320
Yeah, but it's next week.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:32.140
Ren...

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:32.860
What?

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:38.710
If you really don't want to go to 
the dentist, you don't have to.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:41.710
I mean, you really should, but...

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:43.100
Which is it?

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.970
Japanese people can be so confusing.

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:49.220
But you said you didn't want a snack.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:50.770
At this rate, you'll say

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:53.230
you won't even eat dinner 
until you see the dentist.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:55.600
You brush your teeth properly.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.230
Don't worry about cavities.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.230
You're the one who's worried about them.

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:00.230
Huh?

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:05.350
I didn't know you were worried that 
my tooth decay might infect you.

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:08.490
I'm sorry. I'll go see the dentist.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:10.160
I'll be careful from now on.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:15.200
<i>Sometimes I'm a really insensitive idiot.</i>

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:18.000
<i>Unfortunately, today is one of those days.</i>

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.000
Wha—

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.210
Sorry. I know.

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:24.510
But I'll die if I don't kiss you right now.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:25.950
That's not—

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:30.710
Bro, you idiot.

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:34.020
You ditched your café to do 
this to the baby brother?

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:35.200
Huh?

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.020
Aki.

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:38.590
Thanks. Haru's being weird.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.990
Wait, Ren! Where are you going? Ren!

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:46.950
It's so busy.

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:49.780
Do you think he took too much time off work?

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:52.880
He couldn't help it. He was injured.

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:57.640
Yeah, but a lot of customers are using 
it as an excuse to talk to Haru-san.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:01.440
I heard you were injured. 
Are you all right?

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:04.370
It's completely better now. I'm fine.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:16.850
You work at Souryou?

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:22.310
Yeah. I'd been staying in the
student dorms until recently.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:25.930
But living among all those rich kids 
was kinda uncomfortable.

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:28.820
I'm glad I was able to find 
a room here so quickly.

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:32.830
Well, you are a teacher at the school 
of one of my former tenants.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.760
I'll give you a discount on the rent.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.330
A former tenant?

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:42.000
<i>Our school is full of rich kids 
from top percentile families.</i>

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.840
<i>Who on earth would've lived 
in this run-down apartment?</i>

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:48.300
You can ask him about the details.

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:51.300
Are you finished cleaning?

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.300
Yeah. I aired out the apartment, too.

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:56.810
<i>I've heard this voice before.</i>

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:02.310
Oh, you're the new resident?

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.690
You know each other?

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.150
He's my school doctor.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:09.070
<i>The devil lives here!</i>

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:13.300
What's wrong, Shima?

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:16.950
I feel like I've seen that girl 
sitting at the counter before.

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:21.500
Come to think of it, she was sitting in 
the same place by herself yesterday.

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:24.160
What, Ikuyoshi?

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:25.920
It's her.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.960
The girl from the marriage 
meeting photo Haru-san had.

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:32.440
Didn't he already turn that down?

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:34.150
You're right...

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:37.300
I wonder if he's noticed.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:39.890
I guess not.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.370
Not my problem.

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:47.860
So? What do you want from me 
first thing in the morning?

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:50.340
It's not morning. It's afternoon.

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:53.910
Should a school doctor be 
living such an unhealthy life?

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:56.370
Does sarcasm not even 
work against this kid?

00:07:56.370 --> 00:08:00.870
Takamura

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:59.710
By the way, I couldn't read the 
characters on your nameplate.

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:00.870
How do you read it?

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:04.310
It's Takamura. Takamura Shirou.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:09.880
You didn't even know the name of the 
school doctor who's been taking care of you?

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:14.910
Oh, right. Yesterday, when I told Haru about 
the school doctor who's been taking care of me,

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:16.690
he told me to bring this.

00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:17.890
It's a housewarming gift.

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.390
A housewarming gift?

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:25.800
You should eat it before it goes bad.

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:31.080
<i>Damn... I feel like I'd accidentally 
answer any of the devil's questions.</i>

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:33.720
Lately he's been into cooking Thai food.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.160
I hope he's not bad at it.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:36.410
I'll gladly have some.

00:08:36.710 --> 00:08:39.960
You can keep eating, but I have a question.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:44.670
<i>There it is! The devil's question attack!</i>

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:49.050
I thought I told you that what dudes do 
together is outside my area of expertise.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:50.570
We can talk about that another time.

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:51.750
Another time?!

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:54.170
I have a more general question today.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:59.100
What kind of sex life does 
an average adult man lead?

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.680
A man like you, for instance.

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:06.910
<i>The devil is truly a devil through and through.</i>

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:14.670
Huh? Ren-kun?

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:19.070
Uh... Mori-sensei?

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:22.130
I'm so glad I ran into you.

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:25.020
I got lost after I entered the park.

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:26.330
Are you here to see Haru?

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:29.340
Hardly. Mikiko-san asked me to come.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:32.340
Apparently, they went 
to pick peaches together.

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:37.340
They sent a bunch to the hospital, 
and I heard you like peaches.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:40.600
Haru-kun told me during our 
counseling session the other day.

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:43.500
All Japanese fruit is good.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:46.000
Is Haru-kun busy with work?

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:50.440
He hasn't scheduled his 
next counseling session yet.

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:53.040
He only takes Sunday off.

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:55.070
He has customers lining up on weekdays, too.

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:56.860
It's hard for him to get away.

00:09:57.220 --> 00:10:01.120
Besides, it must be difficult to get 
Haru to tell you how he really feels.

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:05.260
He hides himself so well that he doesn't 
even realize his own feelings.

00:10:05.890 --> 00:10:09.800
<i>My, my. The twins were sharp, too,</i>

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:12.630
<i>but their youngest brother is exceptional.</i>

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:14.730
Is something worrying you?

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:18.820
The anniversary of the deaths of the 
Kaidou family parents is coming up,

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:21.190
but Haru hasn't said anything about it.

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:25.490
I've never been to their graves.

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:28.150
I don't even know where they are.

00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:30.660
This isn't normal, is it?

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.070
<i>He's right.</i>

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:37.650
Ren-kun, do you remember 
the Kaidou family parents?

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:41.720
No. I only met them a few times 
at the orphanage in Canada.

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:46.190
But I remember them smiling 
happily when they looked at me.

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:50.340
I wasn't even a cute kid, 
so I found it strange.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:53.670
Most adults would get mad at me.

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:57.930
Sometimes I remember them 
when I see Haru's smiling face.

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:02.190
Haru always smiles the same way they did.

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:10.070
Sorry, Ren-kun. I'm being 
called back to the hospital.

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:13.690
Could you let Haru-kun know 
these are from Mikiko-san?

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:15.940
I'll visit the café another time.

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:17.250
Got it.

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:20.780
Also, you're just like Haru-kun.

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:23.890
That must've been what made 
the Kaidou family parents smile.

00:11:23.890 --> 00:11:24.450
Huh?

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:25.860
See you later!

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:29.460
<i>I think he just said something I can't ignore.</i>

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:32.580
Haru?

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:34.920
What are you doing in the middle of the night?

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:37.550
Since we were given so many peaches,

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:40.550
I thought I'd make some sherbet and tarts.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:42.560
But they're good the way they are.

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:46.310
You won't get tired of them 
if you have a few varieties.

00:11:46.610 --> 00:11:47.750
I wouldn't get tired of them.

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:50.920
Fine. If you want to eat 
some right now, get a plate.

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:51.810
I'll peel one for you.

00:11:52.090 --> 00:11:53.620
I can eat them as they are.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:55.920
You haven't been this stubborn 
about food in a while.

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:57.170
Give me a minute.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:59.820
Open your mouth. Be careful.

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:05.190
<i>This is kind of a dirty image, isn't it?</i>

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:09.590
Our eldest brother, 
getting all hot over peaches.

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:12.330
He gets turned on by the most obscure stuff.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.790
Anyway, peel me some peaches.

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:17.290
Stop reading my mind!

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:20.550
You'll break my glass heart!

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:22.680
That's some pretty thin glass.

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:24.410
I can see right through it.

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:25.640
What did you say?!

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:27.150
Shut up, bro!

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:28.850
<i>There's no way I'm like him.</i>

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:29.470
Could you peel us some peaches already?

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:31.060
If you make me mad, my glass heart...

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:33.690
<i>I'm the complete opposite of Haru.</i>

00:12:34.180 --> 00:12:36.250
<i>We probably want different things, too.</i>

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:41.910
<i>Haru's satisfied to always have his "family" 
by his side, but that's not enough for me.</i>

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:46.390
<i>How can I make Haru mine?</i>

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:53.160
I'm thinking about getting 
my cooking license.

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:56.130
What? Do you want to open 
a restaurant like I did?

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:59.060
Being an owner seems hard.

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:02.170
I'm no good with money, either.

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:05.270
But working at a café is my dream.

00:13:05.270 --> 00:13:07.700
This place seems like 
so much fun every day.

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:07.730
Is today the fifth day?

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:09.680
Her attendance has been perfect.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:09.680
You're right.

00:13:10.070 --> 00:13:11.680
Who has perfect attendance?

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:14.500
That girl talking to our brother.

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:16.960
Do you remember the girl in 
the marriage meeting photo?

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:19.690
Oh, yeah. Didn't Haru already turn her down?

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:21.710
Our bro's so dumb,

00:13:21.710 --> 00:13:25.840
he doesn't even realize the person 
he's talking to right now is her.

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:27.200
I know!

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:30.080
Why don't you let me work here?

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:31.120
Huh?

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:34.330
I need to save money for cooking school, too.

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:38.560
I'm sure I'd learn a lot working here.

00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:36.490
She's tough.

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:40.840
Nah, all the women our bro's dated 
before have been like that.

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:40.140
Can I?

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:43.740
<i>I haven't made any progress.</i>

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:45.840
<i>I always have to watch the same thing.</i>

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:48.960
<i>There's no end to the women 
trying to seduce Haru.</i>

00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:52.600
<i>After all, Haru doesn't belong to me.</i>

00:13:56.300 --> 00:13:57.180
Hey.

00:13:57.180 --> 00:13:59.100
Natsuo, you're here?

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:01.700
Haru told me to come and have lunch.

00:14:02.210 --> 00:14:03.840
Why are you making a weird face?

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:05.360
Sorry my face is weird.

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:07.890
The café's as busy as ever, huh?

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:10.370
Is being served by a former 
host its selling point?

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:14.890
No, although it's true that a lot of 
women come to the café for Haru.

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:16.620
The twins stand out, too.

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:21.870
Isn't it time you forgot about your 
stupid brother and got a girlfriend?

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:24.270
Your precious summer 
vacation will be over soon.

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:29.480
Natsuo, how old were you when 
you first did it with a woman?

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:33.470
I was younger than you. 
She was one year older, and—

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:37.390
Wait, whoa! I didn't expect 
you to ask me that!

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:38.020
Why not?

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:41.790
Why not? You don't seem 
interested in that kind of thing.

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:44.940
Haru and the twins don't talk 
about that in front of you, either.

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:46.030
You're just a kid.

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:53.050
Didn't you just say you were younger than 
me when you first did it with a woman?

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:55.410
That's not what I'm talking about.

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:58.480
You and I grew up in different environments.

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:01.110
Anyway, you've got a cute face.

00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:04.170
Once you get a little taller, 
women will start coming to you.

00:15:04.810 --> 00:15:07.330
I'd love to see Haru's face 
when that starts happening.

00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:08.660
...soon enough.

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:09.170
What?

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:12.720
That's not nearly soon enough.

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:15.030
I want to grow up faster.

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:21.620
Are you inviting me to do 
naughty things with you?

00:15:22.990 --> 00:15:27.190
I told you, I didn't give her a job.

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:31.430
I can't believe you always get 
caught up with women like that.

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:34.780
You didn't realize she was the girl from 
the marriage meeting photo, did you?

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:36.580
You could've told me.

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:39.580
I can't believe you watched 
silently for five days.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:46.560
What are you two doing?!

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:47.260
Nothing.

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:48.460
We were just talking.

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:53.120
Ren, you can't just sit on men's laps!

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:54.550
I do it to you.

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:55.680
I'm different!

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:56.470
You're so selfish.

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:59.100
Haru, can I stay over tonight?

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:00.610
Well, I guess...

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:04.480
Okay, I'll be drinking in the 
bar until dinner's ready.

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:05.460
Ren.

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:08.360
Come visit my place sometime.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:11.990
You can't move on to the next stage in a game 
until you beat the one you're on, right?

00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:15.150
What game?

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:15.990
I don't know.

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:23.300
<i>Last summer, when I came back from a 
two-week summer camp, Haru was gone.</i>

00:16:24.030 --> 00:16:28.340
<i>He didn't leave a note. His suitcase, 
passport, and car were still there.</i>

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:31.510
<i>I stayed up all night waiting for him.</i>

00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:35.510
<i>The next morning, he came back 
like nothing had happened.</i>

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:39.010
<i>He didn't even ask why my eyes were red.</i>

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:41.660
<i>His hair was slightly damp.</i>

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:44.520
<i>There was a strange, sweet 
smell coming from him.</i>

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:51.420
<i>That was the moment I was forced 
to realize I was still a child.</i>

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:57.160
I'm really sorry about yesterday.

00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:00.000
My aunt told you about me, didn't she?

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.430
Oh, well...

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:02.660
<i>She's tough!</i>

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:07.420
I just really wanted to help you here.

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:11.710
I thought you'd get to know me if I were around.

00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:13.420
How formidable.

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:16.790
Will you at least let me help during lunch?

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:18.500
You don't need to pay me.

00:17:19.070 --> 00:17:19.810
Haru.

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:21.870
Make me a gin and tonic.

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:23.690
With extra limes.

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:27.560
But I run the café.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:30.320
Who cares? Don't be stingy. Oh, also...

00:17:30.850 --> 00:17:33.220
The Anzai sisters are here.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:39.070
All your female friends are so flamboyant.

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:41.550
They seem like they party a lot.

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:44.080
They all have proper jobs.

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:48.080
Kiyo operates a number of 
restaurants, including this place.

00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:51.620
The Anzai sisters run a mail-order company.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:54.340
They're busier than me and make more money.

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:57.550
B-But once women get married, their jobs...

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:01.350
Both of my parents worked.

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:05.600
And they seem more likely to have 
house-husbands than be housewives.

00:18:05.990 --> 00:18:07.790
I wish I could be a house-husband.

00:18:11.410 --> 00:18:14.860
Huh? Brother, where's that girl?

00:18:15.230 --> 00:18:18.720
She disappeared when I started 
talking about house-husbands.

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:20.370
I'm opposed to sexism.

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:26.810
Ren, let's take a break.

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:35.080
How's the peach tart?

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:37.620
It's good. The sherbet was good, too.

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:38.630
Really?

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:40.140
Hey, Ren.

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:44.140
What were you doing here 
with Natsuo yesterday?

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:46.520
We were just talking.

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:48.160
That's unusual.

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:51.520
You don't do that kind of 
stuff with Aki and Shima.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:53.300
So what?

00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:55.680
So what? Well, uh...

00:18:56.030 --> 00:19:00.600
It's, well, you know... 
not something you normally do.

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:02.030
What does that make you, then?

00:19:02.310 --> 00:19:05.040
We're special, of course.

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:08.590
Haru...

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:12.600
Do you want to have sex?

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:15.810
You've been all about that lately.

00:19:15.810 --> 00:19:17.560
If you're horny, I'll give you a hand.

00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:20.180
It's not that. I want to have sex with you.

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:22.150
Why are you in such a hurry?

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:26.060
You just learned how to masturbate 
the other day. You're so brazen.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:27.920
That's irrelevant.

00:19:27.920 --> 00:19:31.560
Plenty of people around me 
have already experienced it.

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:35.810
Ren, where do you hear about these things?

00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:39.030
Besides, aren't those mostly 
heterosexual encounters?

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:43.200
No, wait. You're definitely not 
ready to be with a woman, either.

00:19:43.610 --> 00:19:44.700
Why?

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:46.210
<i>What is this?</i>

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:48.300
<i>I'm scared I'll get caught up in his pace!</i>

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:51.920
Either way, you're still a kid.

00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:56.350
You'd say that no matter how old I was.

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:58.950
What will make you stop 
treating me like a child?

00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:00.670
What would...

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:05.280
<i>No matter what I do, that Ren 
follows me around inside my head.</i>

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:10.210
<i>He may have grown, but the impression 
he made then hasn't changed.</i>

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:12.690
<i>But has it really?</i>

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:15.190
Fine. Forget it.

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:19.170
Determining maturity based 
on age alone is stupid.

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:21.570
It's not even your decision to make!

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:23.150
Ren...

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:24.740
Where are you going, Ren?

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:25.530
I'm going out.

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:31.040
<i>That brat doesn't even understand how I feel.</i>

00:20:31.400 --> 00:20:34.060
<i>He's still just a kid.</i>

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:39.550
Huh?

00:20:39.830 --> 00:20:40.550
Ren?

00:20:41.990 --> 00:20:44.530
I'm about to leave for work.

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:45.470
That's fine.

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:47.440
Can I stay here tonight?

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:48.830
Sure, but...

00:20:49.530 --> 00:20:51.630
Did you want to pick up 
where we left off yesterday?

00:20:51.630 --> 00:20:54.440
Where did you tell Haru you were going?

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:56.440
Fine.

00:20:56.960 --> 00:20:58.890
I'll call Haru.

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:02.730
I'll be back after midnight, 
so find something to eat.

00:21:02.730 --> 00:21:03.650
Okay.

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:14.910
<i>Now that I think about it, it's easier for me 
to be around people who aren't Haru.</i>

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:17.520
<i>I don't need them to like me.</i>

00:21:18.030 --> 00:21:21.470
<i>I don't need to worry about 
what they're thinking.</i>

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:23.430
I'm tired.

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:28.180
What? Ren's staying over? Why?

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:30.680
I can go pick him up.

00:21:31.050 --> 00:21:32.960
<i>You're so overprotective.</i>

00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:35.130
<i>What are you so worried about?</i>

00:21:35.130 --> 00:21:37.440
But he didn't say anything earlier.

00:21:37.760 --> 00:21:43.540
Haru, it upsets him when 
you treat him like a little kid.

00:21:43.540 --> 00:21:45.950
<i>What? Ren's mad?</i>

00:21:46.170 --> 00:21:47.950
<i>Are you stupid?</i>

00:21:48.190 --> 00:21:51.720
<i>If you want to keep Ren around forever, 
this is having the opposite effect.</i>

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:55.160
I hope you don't regret it.

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:40.220
Next Time
